      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright (c) 2009 Elsevier Ireland Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "Matrix metalloproteinase-3 and its gene, MMP3, have been implicated in atherosclerotic diseases of coronary arteries. We conducted a haplotype analysis to examine the role of common variation of MMP3 in myocardial infarction (MI) and a meta-analysis to combine available evidence on the association between the 5A/6A polymorphism (rs3025058) and coronary diseases."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "METHODS AND RESULTS",
            "content": "Genotype distributions of haplotype-tagging single nucleotide polymorphisms (rs522616, rs650108, rs569444, rs635746) and rs3025058 were not significantly different between a group with MI (n=3657) and a control group (n=1211) (p> or =0.24). Five major haplotypes were established, and their frequencies were not substantially different between the case and control groups (p> or =0.11). In a meta-analysis of 15 studies (10,061 cases, 8048 controls), the overall risk of coronary disease was not different between the carriers of the 5A allele and 6A6A genotype of rs3025058 (OR, 1.00; 95% CI, 0.85-1.19). Moderate trends of a reduced risk in the 5A allele carriers of European ancestry (OR, 0.87; 95% CI, 0.76-1.00) and an increased risk in the 5A allele carriers from East Asia (OR, 1.33; 95% CI, 0.94-1.90) were observed."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "Individual polymorphisms and haplotypes of MMP3 were not associated with MI in a German case-control study. Evidence was obtained to suggest different risk effects of rs3025058 between Europeans and East Asians."
          }
        ]
      },
